{"name":"Razee","hex":"#7197cb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"razee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An armed ship with its upper deck cut away, and thus reduced to the next inferior rate, such as a seventy-four cut down to a frigate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut (a ship) down to a smaller number of decks, and thus to an inferior rate or class.","To trim or abridge by cutting off parts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/razee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Razee","blocks":[{"text":"A razee or razée is a sailing ship that has been cut down (razeed) to reduce the number of decks. The word is derived from the French vaisseau rasé, meaning a razed ship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/The_arrival_of_the_frigate_H.M.S._%27Anson%27_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-The_arrival_of_the_frigate_H.M.S._%27Anson%27_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Razee","wikidata":"Q1459896"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Sovereign_of_the_Seas%281637%29%3B_Warship%3B_100_guns.jpg/500px-Sovereign_of_the_Seas%281637%29%3B_Warship%3B_100_guns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Sovereign_of_the_Seas%281637%29%3B_Warship%3B_100_guns.jpg/500px-Sovereign_of_the_Seas%281637%29%3B_Warship%3B_100_guns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ship model of Sovereign of the Seas","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASovereign_of_the_Seas(1637)%3B_Warship%3B_100_guns.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Capture_of_La_Virginie_by_HMS_Indefatigable_by_Moonlight%2C_April_21%2C_1796.jpg/500px-Capture_of_La_Virginie_by_HMS_Indefatigable_by_Moonlight%2C_April_21%2C_1796.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia